Institutional Smart Money Concepts (SMC) Execution & Auditing Bot - Architecture Blueprint1. System Overview & ObjectiveAn institutional-grade, multi-timeframe algorithmic trading engine deployed on an AWS EC2 instance. It continuously polls live market feeds via the Twelve Data API for EUR/USD and XAU/USD, filters market noise using structural Smart Money Concepts (SMC), executes automated risk-to-reward tracking, sends real-time Telegram alerts, and logs all trade lifecycles into a local CSV audit report.2. End-to-End Execution FlowPlaintext4H Macro Bias Determination 
       ↓
1H External Liquidity Sweep Detection (Macro Swing Pools)
       ↓
15M Structure Confirmation (FVG + BOS / CHoCH Validation)
       ↓
1M Order Block Entry Trigger & ATR-Buffered Stop Loss
       ↓
Dynamic Take Profit Targeting (Opposing Macro Liquidity Pools)
       ↓
Active Trade Lifecycle Tracking & CSV Auditing (TP1/TP2/TP3/SL)
Step-by-Step Logic Breakdown:Multi-Timeframe Data Fetching (SmartRotatorFetcher):Rotates across multiple Twelve Data API keys to bypass rate limits.Pulls data across four distinct timeframes: 4H (Macro Bias), 1H (Liquidity Pools), 15M (Structural Confluence), and 1M (Execution & Tracking).Phase 1 — 4H Macro Bias Analysis:Evaluates the last 10 swing highs and lows on the 4H chart.Establishes overall market direction: BULLISH (Higher Highs & Higher Lows) or BEARISH.Phase 2 — 1H External Liquidity Sweep:Scans the 1H timeframe past immediate internal chop to identify deep external macro swing liquidity pools (e.g., Previous Day Lows/Highs or major swing shelves).Verifies if the current 1H candle has swept/breached these external levels. If un-swept, the bot remains in a HOLD state.Phase 3 — 15M Structural Validation (SETUP_FORMING):Once external liquidity is swept, the engine looks at the 15M timeframe.Checks for a valid Fair Value Gap (FVG) imbalance and Break of Structure (BOS) / Change of Character (CHoCH) alignment matching the 4H bias.Broadcasts a Telegram advance warning (SETUP_FORMING) alerting that an institutional footprint is validated and the engine is waiting for a 1M retracement into the Order Block / POI.Phase 4 — 1M Entry & Risk Configuration (TRIGGERED):When price retraces into the 15M/1M Point of Interest (POI), the bot triggers execution.Stop-Loss (SL): Calculated using a recent lower-timeframe swing extreme buffered by an Average True Range (ATR) multiplier to prevent wick hunting.Take-Profits (TP1, TP2, TP3): Dynamically derived by scanning opposing macro liquidity pools (such as external swing highs/lows or Weak Highs) rather than using arbitrary fixed pip targets.Position Sizing Matrix: Calculates potential risk-reward ratios and multi-lot PnL breakdowns ($0.01$ to $1.0$ lots).Phase 5 — Active Trade Auditing & CSV Logging (trade_history.csv):Automatically tracks open trades across every polling cycle.Monitors live 1M closing prices against active targets.Instantly fires Telegram notifications and logs events to trade_history.csv when:A trade is opened (ENTRY)Take Profit targets are reached (TP1_HIT, TP2_HIT, TP3_HIT_CLOSED)Stop Loss is breached (SL_HIT)3. Technology Stack & EnvironmentLanguage: Python 3Data Provider: Twelve Data API (via rotation handler)Libraries: Pandas, NumPy, RequestsNotifications: Telegram Bot API (parse_mode='Markdown')Infrastructure: AWS EC2 t3.micro instance running continuous polling loops (run_bot.sh)Data Storage: Local structured CSV audit trail (trade_history.csv)